WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.257
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B two, Book two.

2
00:00:05.557 --> 00:00:09.211
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.511 --> 00:00:15.333
Unit twelve: Financial Literacy. Today you will give advice with 'If I were you, I would…'.

4
00:00:15.633 --> 00:00:18.180
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.133 --> 00:00:22.355
Part one: words. You will learn twelve new words.

6
00:00:23.217 --> 00:00:24.427
Compound interest.

7
00:00:25.417 --> 00:00:29.878
Compound interest means interest you earn on your savings and on past interest.

8
00:00:30.483 --> 00:00:33.238
Compound interest makes savings grow fast.

9
00:00:33.850 --> 00:00:36.955
Your turn. Say: Compound interest.

10
00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:41.405
Compound interest.

11
00:00:42.150 --> 00:00:43.360
Diversify.

12
00:00:44.350 --> 00:00:47.627
Diversify means to spread money across different things.

13
00:00:48.217 --> 00:00:50.344
Smart investors diversify.

14
00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:53.626
Your turn. Say: Diversify.

15
00:00:56.467 --> 00:00:57.712
Diversify.

16
00:00:58.450 --> 00:00:59.765
Risk tolerance.

17
00:01:00.750 --> 00:01:03.980
Risk tolerance means how much risk you can accept.

18
00:01:04.583 --> 00:01:07.535
Young people often have a higher risk tolerance.

19
00:01:08.150 --> 00:01:10.953
Your turn. Say: Risk tolerance.

20
00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:15.254
Risk tolerance.

21
00:01:16.017 --> 00:01:17.401
Financial planning.

22
00:01:18.417 --> 00:01:22.146
Financial planning means deciding how to use money for the future.

23
00:01:22.750 --> 00:01:24.982
Financial planning starts with a budget.

24
00:01:25.583 --> 00:01:28.294
Your turn. Say: Financial planning.

25
00:01:31.133 --> 00:01:32.634
Financial planning.

26
00:01:33.383 --> 00:01:34.593
Passive income.

27
00:01:35.583 --> 00:01:38.697
Passive income means money you earn without daily work.

28
00:01:39.283 --> 00:01:41.469
Rent from a house is passive income.

29
00:01:42.083 --> 00:01:44.666
Your turn. Say: Passive income.

30
00:01:47.500 --> 00:01:48.640
Passive income.

31
00:01:49.383 --> 00:01:50.663
Credit score.

32
00:01:51.650 --> 00:01:54.938
Credit score means a number that shows if you repay loans.

33
00:01:55.550 --> 00:01:57.933
Paying on time improves your credit score.

34
00:01:58.517 --> 00:02:01.378
Your turn. Say: Credit score.

35
00:02:04.233 --> 00:02:05.351
Credit score.

36
00:02:06.117 --> 00:02:07.153
Debt management.

37
00:02:08.150 --> 00:02:11.322
Debt management means controlling and paying back money you owe.

38
00:02:11.917 --> 00:02:14.427
Debt management stops loans from growing.

39
00:02:15.017 --> 00:02:18.041
Your turn. Say: Debt management.

40
00:02:20.900 --> 00:02:22.215
Debt management.

41
00:02:22.950 --> 00:02:24.729
Investment portfolio.

42
00:02:25.717 --> 00:02:29.005
Investment portfolio means all the investments you own.

43
00:02:29.617 --> 00:02:32.777
Her investment portfolio includes gold and shares.

44
00:02:33.383 --> 00:02:36.709
Your turn. Say: Investment portfolio.

45
00:02:39.567 --> 00:02:41.531
Investment portfolio.

46
00:02:42.283 --> 00:02:43.900
Retirement savings.

47
00:02:44.883 --> 00:02:48.206
Retirement savings means money saved for when you stop working.

48
00:02:48.817 --> 00:02:50.735
Start retirement savings early.

49
00:02:51.350 --> 00:02:54.536
Your turn. Say: Retirement savings.

50
00:02:57.400 --> 00:02:58.958
Retirement savings.

51
00:02:59.717 --> 00:03:01.368
Economic literacy.

52
00:03:02.383 --> 00:03:06.113
Economic literacy means understanding how the economy works.

53
00:03:06.717 --> 00:03:09.726
Economic literacy helps you understand prices.

54
00:03:10.317 --> 00:03:13.840
Your turn. Say: Economic literacy.

55
00:03:16.700 --> 00:03:18.189
Economic literacy.

56
00:03:18.950 --> 00:03:20.241
Wealth building.

57
00:03:21.250 --> 00:03:23.958
Wealth building means growing your money over time.

58
00:03:24.550 --> 00:03:26.642
Wealth building takes patience.

59
00:03:27.250 --> 00:03:29.635
Your turn. Say: Wealth building.

60
00:03:32.500 --> 00:03:33.745
Wealth building.

61
00:03:34.483 --> 00:03:35.775
Budget discipline.

62
00:03:36.783 --> 00:03:39.816
Budget discipline means sticking to your spending plan.

63
00:03:40.417 --> 00:03:42.985
Budget discipline means no impulse buying.

64
00:03:43.583 --> 00:03:46.491
Your turn. Say: Budget discipline.

65
00:03:49.333 --> 00:03:50.834
Budget discipline.

66
00:03:51.633 --> 00:03:55.331
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

67
00:03:56.183 --> 00:04:00.113
Visal, I got my first salary. What should I do?

68
00:04:01.217 --> 00:04:05.480
If I were you, I would start saving early.

69
00:04:06.583 --> 00:04:07.828
Why so early?

70
00:04:08.917 --> 00:04:13.125
Because of compound interest. Your money grows on its growth.

71
00:04:14.217 --> 00:04:15.380
Anything else?

72
00:04:16.483 --> 00:04:20.131
If I were you, I would diversify and avoid debt.

73
00:04:21.267 --> 00:04:22.604
Part three: grammar.

74
00:04:23.450 --> 00:04:26.436
Grammar focus: Conditional advice (if I were you).

75
00:04:26.736 --> 00:04:27.935
Look at the pattern.

76
00:04:28.650 --> 00:04:31.404
If I were you, I would start saving early.

77
00:04:32.317 --> 00:04:35.593
If I were you, I wouldn't borrow money for a new phone.

78
00:04:36.483 --> 00:04:38.622
If I were you, I would make a budget.

79
00:04:39.567 --> 00:04:44.622
Always say 'If I were you', not 'If I was you'. Then use 'would' + base verb.

80
00:04:45.383 --> 00:04:49.661
Be careful! Don't say: If I was you, I will save early.

81
00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:54.076
Say: If I were you, I would save early.

82
00:04:54.376 --> 00:04:56.224
Say 'If I were you, I would…'.

83
00:04:57.033 --> 00:04:59.570
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

84
00:05:00.367 --> 00:05:01.519
Money Smart.

85
00:05:01.819 --> 00:05:05.629
Financial literacy helps teenagers make wise choices.

86
00:05:06.633 --> 00:05:09.747
Compound interest rewards people who save early.

87
00:05:10.733 --> 00:05:13.778
Budget discipline and debt management protect your future.

88
00:05:14.767 --> 00:05:18.043
Smart investors diversify their investment portfolio.

89
00:05:19.033 --> 00:05:22.043
If I were you, I would start wealth building today.

90
00:05:23.133 --> 00:05:27.077
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

91
00:05:27.917 --> 00:05:30.299
If I were you, I blank save money.

92
00:05:30.599 --> 00:05:33.974
A, would. B, will. C, am.

93
00:05:37.533 --> 00:05:39.010
The answer is A: would.

94
00:05:40.150 --> 00:05:43.345
A number that shows if you repay loans is a credit blank.

95
00:05:43.645 --> 00:05:46.904
A, score. B, income. C, plan.

96
00:05:50.467 --> 00:05:52.327
The answer is A: score.

97
00:05:53.483 --> 00:05:56.098
To spread money across different things is to blank.

98
00:05:56.398 --> 00:06:00.319
A, diversify. B, budget. C, retire.

99
00:06:03.867 --> 00:06:06.261
The answer is A: diversify.

100
00:06:07.467 --> 00:06:10.607
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

101
00:06:11.450 --> 00:06:15.121
Why is financial literacy important for teenagers to learn early?

102
00:06:23.917 --> 00:06:25.254
Now listen to Visal.

103
00:06:25.554 --> 00:06:34.453
It is important because good habits start young. If I were a teenager with no savings, I would make a budget and save a little every week.

104
00:06:34.753 --> 00:06:36.799
Excellent answer, Visal!

105
00:06:37.683 --> 00:06:42.356
Great work! Now you can use twelve new words and conditional advice (if i were you).

106
00:06:42.656 --> 00:06:47.572
Today's value is planning ahead. Make a plan and take small steps every day.

107
00:06:47.872 --> 00:06:50.373
See you in Unit thirteen. Goodbye!

108
00:06:50.673 --> 00:06:53.593
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

